    [vllm#58411](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/58411)
    `randomize_inputs`;
    [vllm#57169](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/57169) split
    metadata-builder creation and changed `AttentionGroup`;
    [vllm#60517](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/60517) removed
    the SP pass and the `tensor_parallel_size` argument | Forward
    `randomize_inputs` unconditionally, build `AttentionGroup` without
    positional builders and call
    `initialize_metadata_builders`/`_init_device_metadata_providers` on
    main, inline the SP-aware lcm, resolve cudagraph sizes without
    `tensor_parallel_size`, treat `update_pass_config` as a no-op on main
    and collapse 310P drafter kernel block sizes to an int |
    | `vllm_ascend/worker/v2/block_table.py` |
    [vllm#57169](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/57169) dropped
    `kernel_block_sizes`/`blocks_per_kv_block` from `BlockTables` and
    stopped expanding block ids | Version-split `__init__` to restore the
    kernel-block layout (sizes, `blocks_per_kv_block`, expanded rows,
    kernel-size tensor) and override `append_block_ids` on main |
    | `vllm_ascend/worker/v2/model_runner.py` |
    [vllm#58411](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/58411)
    `randomize_inputs`; main's rejection sampler takes invalidation state
    and needs the new `InputBatch` fields | Forward `randomize_inputs` and
    `max_seq_len_np` unconditionally, skip grammar application on empty
    logits and pass `grammar_invalid_drafts` output into the main rejection
    sampler |
    | `vllm_ascend/worker/v2/model_states/mamba_hybrid.py` | vLLM main
    removed `MambaHybridModelState._ensure_align_ctx` and moved
    align-context creation into `initialize_kv_cache`, so the first forward
    aborted with `AttributeError: ... has no attribute '_ensure_align_ctx'`
    / `AssertionError` when the context was absent | Define
    `_ensure_align_ctx` per lane: delegate on v0.31.0, lazily (re)create the
    align context on main from the forward context |
    | `vllm_ascend/worker/v2/pcp_manager.py` | vLLM main made
    `shard_decode_requests` a required `PCPManager.__init__` argument and
    `maybe_build_pcp_manager` passes it (`TypeError: ... unexpected keyword
    argument 'shard_decode_requests'`) | Version-split
    `AscendPCPManager.__init__`, accepting and forwarding the flag on main
    while keeping the Ascend buffer setup shared |
    | `vllm_ascend/worker/v2/spec_decode/autoregressive/aclgraph.py` |
    [vllm#60335](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/60335) moved the
    speculator CUDA-graph manager and added `num_speculative_steps` to the
    captured forward | Import `SpeculatorCudaGraphManager` by lane and pass
    `num_speculative_steps` on main |
    | `vllm_ascend/worker/v2/spec_decode/autoregressive/speculator.py` |
    [vllm#60335](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/60335) renamed
    the AR base class and added `num_speculative_steps`;
    [vllm#60754](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/60754) renamed
    `dp_sync` -> `dp_sync_state` (`TypeError:
    AscendAutoRegressiveSpeculator.propose() got an unexpected keyword
    argument 'dp_sync_state'`) | Bind the upstream base class by lane and
    version-split `propose()`/`_propose_impl()` plus
    `_generate_draft`/`_multi_step_decode` so each lane forwards exactly its
    arguments |
    | `vllm_ascend/worker/v2/spec_decode/dflash/speculator.py` |
    [vllm#57169](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/57169) makes the
    DFlash caller forward the physical block size while the Ascend block
    table stays kernel-block addressed (draft KV mismapped, every draft
    rejected);
    [vllm#60335](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/60335)/[vllm#60754](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/60754)
    speculator contract | Version-split `prepare_dflash_inputs_factory`
    (restoring the kernel block size per group on main) and
    `propose()`/`_propose_impl()`, keeping the profiling DP-count guard |
    | `vllm_ascend/worker/v2/spec_decode/dspark/speculator.py` | Same
    speculator contract changes | Same version-split
    `propose()`/`_propose_impl()` adaptation |
    | `vllm_ascend/worker/worker.py` |
    [vllm#58411](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/58411)
    `profile_run` takes `randomize_inputs` | Compute `randomize_inputs` from
    the env flag + DP size and forward it on both `profile_run` calls |
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. This is a CI/main2main compatibility update: behavior on vLLM main
    is unchanged (the restorations only bring the main lane back to the
    v0.31.0 behavior) and the v0.31.0 release lane is preserved.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Unit tests updated per lane; `pytest -sv tests/ut` against both the
    verified
      main commit (`a98247ab`) and the release tag (`v0.31.0`).
    
    
    - vLLM main:
